ses a novel GNN-based distribution matching algorithm. It decouples structures and attributes and simultaneously matches the distribution of respective latent vectors. WGNN developed by Chen et al. (2021) learns node representations in Wasserstein space without any imputation. Jin et al. (2021) propose the HGNN-AC model to learn topological embedding and attribute completion with weighted aggregation. PaGNNs Jiang & Zhang (2020) can reconstruct the missing attributes based on a partial message-propagation scheme. Among them, SAT performs well and has open-source implementations, so we refer to SAT as a primary base model for completing missing node attributes."
